{"created": "2026-10-07T05:35:37.608378+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-10T21:24:52.833389+00:00", "id": 23204212, "conceptrecid": "23204211", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23204212", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23204211", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23204212", "metadata": {"title": "Reduced C*-algebras of the Thompson family: an attributed consequence of nonamenability", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23204212", "publication_date": "2026-10-06", "description": "An attributed consequence note applying OpenAI's nonamenability theorem for standard Thompson F to the published equivalences of Le Boudec and Matte Bon. The reduced group C*-algebras of F, T, the full automorphism group Aut(F), and the abstract commensurator Comm(F) are simple and have their canonical traces as their unique tracial states, by the discrete-group trace theorem of Breuillard, Kalantar, Kennedy and Ozawa. The countable standard circle-overgroup consequence is also recorded. All these simplicity reductions are inherited; T's unique trace was already unconditional. No new simplicity criterion, independent proof of nonamenability, or first-priority claim is made. The conclusions depending on the new input have exactly the same dependency on its validity. The source proof was manually audited; actual Lean source and semantics were inspected, but no fresh Lean kernel build was reproduced owing to insufficient disk space, and the follow-on theorem is not claimed to be formalized. AI tools were used extensively in research, drafting and verification. This preprint has not undergone conventional human peer review or refereeing; automated adversarial audits are not human peer review.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["Thompson groups", "reduced group C*-algebras", "C*-simplicity", "unique trace", "Thompson group F", "Thompson group T", "automorphism group Aut(F)", "abstract commensurator Comm(F)", "nonamenability", "amenable radical", "operator algebras", "discrete groups", "groups of homeomorphisms", "circle actions", "canonical tracial state"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.24033/asens.2361", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s10240-017-0091-2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/openai/math/tree/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Thompsons-group-F-is-nonamenable-September-23-2026", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23204211"}}]}}, "title": "Reduced C*-algebras of the Thompson family: an attributed consequence of nonamenability", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23204212", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23204212", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23204212?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23204212", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23204212", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23204212", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23204212/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23204211", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23204211", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23204211", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23204211", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23204212/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23204212/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23204212/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23204212/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23204212:paper.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23204212:pape